From 5c4f9f234db862b31f9bcf67fbecb444a85b655e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fernando433566 <fernandoblancosanchez08@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:59:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Llamadroid: Android support patches

- Run helper binaries packaged as JNI libraries (lib*_exec.so)
- Look for native libraries next to the binary on Android
- Treat Android GPUs as integrated (shared RAM)
- Recognize llama.cpp's OpenCL backend (Qualcomm Adreno)
- Default to performance cores only on big.LITTLE phone CPUs
- Synergy mode: split layers between CPU and GPU
- Retry once on CPU when an Android GPU load fails
- OLLAMA_RPC_SERVERS: offload layers to other devices via ggml RPC
- load_vision=false to skip the vision projector
- reasoning_budget option (default -1 = unlimited)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
